        <div id="sheen" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            4. Which Sheen for Which Room
          </h2>

          <p>
            Sheen decides how a wall looks and how it wears, often more than the brand does. Higher sheen means a harder, smoother, more washable film, and it also means every dent, patch and roller mark shows. Lower sheen hides imperfections and looks softer, and it is harder to clean without burnishing. Choosing a sheen is a trade between those two, room by room.
          </p>

          <div class="overflow-hidden border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl my-8">
            <div class="overflow-x-auto">
              <table class="w-full text-left">
                <thead class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-200">
                  <tr>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Sheen</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Best rooms</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Why</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  <tr class="bg-white border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Flat</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Ceilings, formal dining rooms, low-traffic adult bedrooms</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Hides imperfections best, but marks easily and can burnish when scrubbed</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Matte</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Living rooms, bedrooms, home offices</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Near-flat look with better washability in premium lines</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-white border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Eggshell</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Most living spaces, hallways in light use</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">The default: slight sheen, wipes clean, still forgiving of wall flaws</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Satin or pearl</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Kids' rooms, hallways, kitchens, bathrooms</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Stands up to regular scrubbing and moisture</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-white border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Semi-gloss</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Trim, doors, cabinets, window casings</td>
